.2), not by systemd mail.\n\n[Service]\nType=oneshot\nUser=root\nExecStart=/bin/bash /usr/local/bin/aria-fleet-feed.sh\n# fleet-check runs up to ~7 min (ear check ~2min + probes); give it\n# headroom. A hung run is killed by the script's own timeout 420.\nTimeoutStartSec=600\nSuccessExitStatus=0\n\n# /usr/lib/systemd/system/service.d/10-timeout-abort.conf\n# This file is part of the systemd package.\n===\n# /etc/systemd/system/aria-fleet-feed.timer\n[Unit]\nDescription=Aria fleet-check feeder timer (every 6h)\n\n[Timer]\n# 6h cadence: the composite signal is fresh enough for an hourly\n# fear organ (max staleness ~7h, well under the 26h fear threshold),\n# and 4 fleet-check runs/day is a tolerable probe load on frigate\n# (each run pulls one recording per camera).\nOnCalendar=00/6:00:00\nPersistent=true\nRandomizedDelaySec=300\nUnit=aria-fleet-feed.service\n\n[Install]\n\n[t+01:45/60:00 c20/300]"}]
